NO THIRD-PARTY CODE OR ASSETS

This project contains no source code, artwork, icons, fonts or other assets from
Apple, Microsoft or any other company. The interface themes are built entirely
from CSS colour and geometry values written for this project. Where a theme
resembles a historical interface, that resemblance is achieved with original
values, not with copied material.

The library format this software reads is Apple's XML property list, parsed with
Python's standard-library `plistlib`. No Apple software, framework or API is
used, and nothing is reverse-engineered or circumvented: the file being read is
one the user already has on their own disk.

Smart playlist rules sit in that file as two binary fields, Smart Info and Smart
Criteria. They are decoded by itunessmart (https://github.com/cvzi/itunes_smartplaylist,
MIT License, copyright cuzi), a separate package installed as a dependency and
not copied into this project. Its reading of the format comes from that project,
not from Apple. This project reverses one detail of that reading, the most/least
direction of three sort orders, after it compared the decoded rules with the
track lists that the same file saved.
